            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ThreadSanitizer observed a data race reached by a fuzz corpus input — two threads accessed the same memory without synchronization and at least one wrote, a bug class ASan and UBSan do not detect. A data race is undefined behavior: it causes torn reads/writes, lost updates, and nondeterministic crashes, and a check-then-act race is a TOCTOU security boundary. bhf replays the ASan pass's corpus through a separate TSan-instrumented build to find these without a second fuzz loop; a race only surfaces when the target spawns threads while processing one input. Synchronize the shared access with a mutex or atomics, or remove the sharing."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "ThreadSanitizer observed a data race reached by a fuzz corpus input — two threads accessed the same memory without synchronization and at least one wrote, a bug class ASan and UBSan do not detect. A data race is undefined behavior: it causes torn reads/writes, lost updates, and nondeterministic crashes, and a check-then-act race is a TOCTOU security boundary. bhf replays the ASan pass's corpus through a separate TSan-instrumented build to find these without a second fuzz loop; a race only surfaces when the target spawns threads while processing one input. Synchronize the shared access with a mutex or atomics, or remove the sharing.\n\n**References:**\n\n- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/362.html\n- https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ThreadSanitizer.html\n",
                "text": "ThreadSanitizer observed a data race reached by a fuzz corpus input — two threads accessed the same memory without synchronization and at least one wrote, a bug class ASan and UBSan do not detect. A data race is undefined behavior: it causes torn reads/writes, lost updates, and nondeterministic crashes, and a check-then-act race is a TOCTOU security boundary. bhf replays the ASan pass's corpus through a separate TSan-instrumented build to find these without a second fuzz loop; a race only surfaces when the target spawns threads while processing one input. Synchronize the shared access with a mutex or atomics, or remove the sharing.\n\nReferences:\n- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/362.html\n- https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ThreadSanitizer.html\n"
